{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/release","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"release","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDivisions","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDivisions","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"release"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"release","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDivisions","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV7releaseAA12MXLDivisionsVSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","title":"release"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/release"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Alters the stopping time of the note from when it would otherwise occur, expressed in divisions. A note that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"starts a tie should not have a release attribute.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/release":{"abstract":[{"text":"Alters the stopping time of the note from when it would otherwise occur, expressed in divisions. A note that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"starts a tie should not have a release attribute.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/release","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/release","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"release","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDivisions","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"release","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"title":"MXLNote","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDivisions":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldivisions","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDivisions","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDivisions"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The divisions type is used to express values in terms of the musical divisions defined by the divisions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element. It is preferred that these be integer values both for MIDI interoperability and to avoid roundoff","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"errors.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDivisions"}],"title":"MXLDivisions"}}}